      "id": 1,
      "text": "Michigan Center was platted as \"Michigan Centre\" in 1837 by Abel Fitch and Paul Ring, though settlers had arrived earlier.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan_Center%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from its proximity to the Michigan meridian, the survey line that split the state.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan_Center%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Michigan Center grew into a mill town on a Grand River tributary, powering early industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan_Center%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Center Lake, formed by a 1911 dam on the Grand River tributary, sits at the community’s northern edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
